sequenceDiagram
    actor U as User
    participant S as Setup assistant
    participant C as ACED
    participant A as Stage agent
    participant H as Existing tools and infrastructure

    Note over U,H: 1. Discover
    U->>S: Project, desired outcome and constraints
    S->>H: Inspect documentation, tools and records
    H-->>S: Available capabilities and current state
    S-->>U: Capabilities map and remaining questions
    U->>S: Resolve business choices and limits

    Note over U,H: 2. Prepare
    S->>S: Prepare configuration, skills and host connections
    S->>H: Configure existing identity, permissions and supervision
    S-->>U: Concrete integration and bounded validation plan
    U->>S: Authorize scope, including standing policy where appropriate

    Note over U,H: 3. Rehearse
    S->>A: Exercise the actual runner in an isolated environment
    A->>H: Test access, checks, evidence writing and controls
    S->>H: Verify independent stopping and interruption recovery
    H-->>S: Receipts and permission results
    Note over S,H: Fix authorized setup issues and repeat failed checks

    Note over U,H: 4. Complete a short real cycle
    S->>C: Start the authorized validation run
    Note over C,H: Before each task: persist inputs and budget, obtain host authorization
    C->>A: Hypothesize
    A->>H: Research approved evidence
    A-->>C: Hypothesis and bounded plan
    C->>C: Accept and freeze plan
    C->>A: Implement
    A->>H: Edit, test and debug
    A-->>C: Candidate and trusted check references
    C->>H: Verify candidate and checks
    C->>A: Experiment - canary scope
    A->>H: Deploy disabled, establish protection, operate canary
    A-->>C: Yield with canary closure evidence
    C->>H: Verify zero, separation and prior execution settlement
    C->>A: Experiment - main scope
    A->>H: Establish main protection, activate once
    A-->>C: Operation reference and checkpoint
    par Durable coordination
        C->>C: Wait and recheck due records
    and Independent protection
        H->>H: Monitor and enforce stopping
    end
    C->>A: Resume for closed-window readout
    A->>H: Inspect the same experiment
    A-->>C: Readout or unsuccessful outcome
    C->>H: Verify closure and evidence
    C->>A: Decide
    A-->>C: Proposed disposition
    C->>H: Verify eligibility and authorization
    C->>A: Execute any required authorized disposition
    A->>H: Apply and observe outcome
    A-->>C: Retained source, learning and assessment
    C->>H: Verify settlement
    C-->>S: Completed cycle and history

    Note over U,H: 5. Validate recovery
    S->>C: Exercise bounded interruption and failure cases
    C->>H: Reconcile original operations and verify stopping
    C-->>S: Recovery evidence and remaining blockers

    Note over U,H: 6. Hand over
    S-->>U: Versioned setup, evidence and operating instructions
    U->>C: Start an authorized goal
    C->>A: Orchestrate subsequent development stages
    C-->>U: Inspectable progress, decisions and learning
    Note over U,H: Setup assistant can exit; independent protection remains available
